YAAP: 77-cdi-sam-hum-fem-law ... (almost) weaponless.
****
It's been a while since I've written a YAAP.  Since my last one, I've
played 12 games (including this one).  I started playing poorly and
forced myself to take a break from nethack.  I can't really call it a
slump though, since 7 of these games ended with an ascension.

I mentioned in another thread that this game felt easier than a normal
katana-wielding samurai.  This is mostly related to weapon and martial
arts skill levels and their associated damage bonuses.  There are
certain sweet spots where martial arts is actually better than either
a single wielded +0 katana or a dual wielded +0 katana and +0
wakizashi pair.  I'll spare you the horrible maths details and give
you the brief rundown with small monster damage in parenthesis.

Expert martial arts (7.00) is comparable to expert +0 katana (7.30)
and basic two-weaponing of a +0 katana and +0 wakizashi (7.27).
Martial arts at master (7.75) is slightly superior to either.  Only
skilled (9.00) and expert (11.63) two-weaponing are better.  Artifact
generation, strength modifiers, and a better off-hand weapon do change
the relationships so don't take it as gospel.

I got the impression from this game that martial arts superiority to
wielded weapons occured during the period of time where offense really
matters.  Essentially, this is the time after monsters tough enough to
give you fits start being generated but before your armour, other
equipment, and hit points are high enough to compensate.

Now, on to the game itself:
****

I set out to ascend a weaponless, genoless, polyless, artiwishless
samurai.  I failed.  I broke weaponless exactly once, on turn 18,554
(Oops!).  Polyobjectless went goodbye while #dip-testing potions.  In
for a penny, in for a pound.  I decided to genocide 'L' and ';'

I started this game by unwielding my weapons, then naming them.  I had
no intention of using either the katana ("Kiri") or wakizashi ("Kana")
but wanted to keep them for roleplaying and stylistic reasons.  I also
named my yumi ("Yuki").

My usual early strategy is to explore the first three levels fully,
mostly looking for enough food to get me to sokoban and hopefully
poison resistance.  After that, I head for sokoban as quickly as
possible.  Once I've completed sokoban I head for minetown, do mines
end, then it's on to the castle.

This game was no different.  There were shops on levels 3 (potion), 4
(general), and 6 (ring).  While heading for sokoban, I got swarmed on
the Oracle level.  That was tense.  The entrance to sokoban was on
Dlvl.6.  I arrived in sokoban around T:1400 and reached the zoo level
(reflection, YEA!) around T:2470

After leaving sokoban, I paid some of the shopkeepers a visit.  The
ring shop had all 4 300gp rings, but I could only afford 2 of them
during my first visit.  They were later identified as polymorph and
polycontrol.  A pot noodle in the Dlvl.05 general store told me this
was a bones level.  This shop also had a cloak of displacement that I
wore until the castle.

Nothing too dramatic happened while I was in the mines.  Minetown
didn't have any magic lamps, and the temple was cross-aligned.  I did
pick up a tinning kit in minetown and mines end was the wine cellar.

Since I didn't have a bag of holding, I let myself be burdened (shame
on me!) as I hauled all the crap I'd picked up from the mines back to
the first level of sokoban.  I know it's a bad habit.  In my defense:
a) much of the stuff was useful later on, and b) staying unburdened
and making 23 trips would drive me insane.

Upon returning to Sokoban I stashed stuff, got unburdened (and tried
to stay that way for most of the remainder of the game).  I kept the
tinning kit, which was probably a mistake (oh well).

It was now time for to make a dash for the Castle.  I set out around T:
9000 with HP:87, AC:-5, reflection, a sack, and a rather limited
inventory.  I did have (or would shortly acquire) rings of polymorph
control, teleport control, free action, and conflict.   I felt very
good about my chances.

Between then and the castle I played hide-and-seek with a co-aligned
unicorn to max my luck.  I lost a bunch of luck by failing to convert
an altar several times in a row (before getting most of it back
shortly afterwords).  I picked up a bugle from some barracks
mercenaries, that was fun.  A little further down, I did some wraith
luring (after an epic jump back and forth session to get unsatiated.
ugh!).

I arrived at the castle on T:13918 with HP:115(115) and AC:-9.  I then
found the upstairs and paid a visit to medusa.  Unfortunately, I
didn't have any means of breaking the statues.  I went back downstairs
and played drawbridge smash.  I did most of it while blind since I
didn't have see invisible yet and there were three demiliches in the
courtyard.  While I was doing all that, Tenaya sent me mail.  That was
way cool!

I got the castle wand of wishing at T:14401.  It turned out to be
(0:1), which was annoying.  I spent my first two wishes on two blessed
scrolls of charging (got 1) and a blessed greased fireproof +2 cloak
of magic resistance.  I then blessed several scrolls of enchant armour
and got my AC down to -17 (I kept 2 scrolls in reserve).

[I'd like to note that the gloves I ascended with were +5 after the
enchantment session.  I had a few disenchanter accidents along the
way.]

Here's where my thinking got wierd.  I had two wishes left (3 with the
wrest) and I still needed a non-amulet source of reflection, a bag of
holding, a marker, and some DSM.  I only wanted to spend one of those
wishes.  So ... I headed back out into and beat up everyone else in
the castle (hoping for a wand of striking, and a shield of reflection
from the Perseus statue).  I got lucky.  I got both.  I then wished up
a bag of holding and said "Hello!" to the dragons.  One dropped scales
(I was prepared to go with mithril).

After cleaning out the store rooms and futzing with inventory I headed
back up to sokoban and the shallow shops.  I wanted to fully explore
those levels and pick up all the stuff I couldn't carry the first
time.  While doing this, on turn 18,554, I saw the message I'd been
dreading since the beginning:

"You begin bashing monsters with your yumi named Yuki. --more--"

Oops!  That sucked.  After ascending, I used vi to search the .ttyrecs
for that phrase.  AFAICT, it only appeared twice.  Once for the actual
hit and once for the message scrollback.  Shortly after this I broke
polyobjectless while #dip-testing potions.

Once the upper dungeon had been mapped and I had gathered all the
tasty loot into my bag (I was burdened, *again*.  I only have the
patience for one trip) I teleported back to the castle.  After an
alchemy session, potion blanking session, and armour enchantment
session I decided to do gehennom.

I want no part of the samurai quest if I don't have an amulet of life
saving and a means of insta-killing Ashikaga Takauji.

So, I level teleported to the VS level on T:22635 with HP:221(221)
AC:-33 and too much crap in my BoH.  I then made my way back to the
VoTD.  I made my way to Orcus town without too much trouble.  I went
upstairs.  "You kick Orcus."  Brought him downstairs.  Whacked him
with a potion of paralysis.  I then killed him (and took his stuff!)
before he had a chance to use his wand.  It was (0:8), this made me
happy.

Then the RNG started making fun of me.  One of the shops in Orcus town
had my inexplicably favorite artifact weapon ... Sunsword.  I also
found two more cloaks of magic resistance in Gehennom.

Vlad also had a wand of death.  Both Baalzebub Asmodeus asked for (and
got) 3 gp.  Some demon summoned Juiblex, so I didn't have to deal with
him in the swamp.
I returned to the castle around T:30500.  After a bit of inventory
(mis)management I felt ready to tackle the Samurai quest.

I didn't gain permission to go on the quest until T:31076.  There
wasn't even a close call.  I made my way to the nemesis level, then
carefully made my way to just outside his meditation spot.  I zapped a
wand of death.  It missed.  I read a scroll of earth while Ashikaga
was busy picking up the Tsurugi then calmly waited for him to teleport
to a square where I could zap him to death.  The 2nd shot killed him.

Up to this point I had neither seen (nor wished for) a magic marker.

After some final preparations it was time for the ascension run.  I
teleported to the portal level, entered Rodney's tower (where a
cockatrice left a corpse), teleported to Rodney's level and made a
nice statue of him before taking his book.

For the sanctum, a level teleport landed me on the left hand side near
the door to the temple.  I was greated by a summon insect storm, so it
took awhile to the high priest and make a statue of him.  The climb to
Dlvl.1 with the AoY was mostly uneventful.

On reaching Dlvl.1 I realized I had only 2 scrolls of gold detection.
Out came the /wishing and I wished for a magic marker.  It was
(0:32).  I spent 9 marker charges on 2 more scrolls.  Re-watching this
part was painful.  I spent far too much time checking and rechecking
my inventory (and then checking it again, for good measure).  I really
should be less anal-retentive about making sure everything is "just
so" before heading off to the planes.

Earth, Air, Fire, and Water were all slightly more eventful than
usual, but not enough so to warrant talking about them in detail.  On
astral, the correct high altar was the 2nd one I visited.  I also
quaffed a !full healing while visiting the first altar, so it got
tense in spots.

-cdi

